&lt;p&gt;Coverage of Services and Supplies Incident to a Physician&#39;s Services&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; Where a physician establishes an office within a nursing home or other institution, coverage of services and supplies furnished in the office must be determined in accordance with the &quot;incident to a physician&#39;s professional service&quot; provision, as in any physician&#39;s office. A physician&#39;s office within an institution must be confined to a separately identified part of the facility which is used solely as the physician&#39;s office and cannot be construed to extend throughout the entire institution. Thus, services performed outside the &quot;office&quot; area would be subject to the coverage rules applicable to services furnished outside the office setting.
&lt;&sol;p&gt;
